Task 2–3 — Launch the EC2 instance
Name: DevOps-Midterm-Exam-2026B
Reuse existing .pem key pair from the course (or create a new one).
No screenshot required for this step per the list — just get it running.

Task 4 — Set the hostname
bash
ssh -i "devops_project_key.pem" ec2-user@<public-ip-or-dns>
sudo su -
nano /etc/hostname
Replace the contents with just:
s123456-midterm-exam-2026b
(swap in student ID). Save (Ctrl+X, Y, Enter), then:
bash
reboot
Wait ~1 minute, SSH back in, and go root again:
bash
ssh -i "devops_project_key.pem" ec2-user@<public-ip-or-dns>
sudo su -
Prompt should now read exactly root@s123456-midterm-exam-2026b:~# — confirm this before taking any further screenshot in the exam, since every terminal screenshot from here on must show this exact hostname.

Task 5 — Generate SSH key pair → 1a.png
bash
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -C "email@example.com"
Press Enter through the prompts (default location, empty passphrase is fine). Screenshot the terminal output of this command — full screen, taskbar with date/time visible.

Task 6 — Add public key to GitHub → 1b.png
bash
cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub
Copy the full output → GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys → New SSH key → paste → give it a title → Add SSH key.

Task 7 — Test SSH connection → 1c.png
bash
ssh -T git@github.com
Type yes if prompted about host authenticity.

Task 8 — Clone the repo → 1d.png
bash
cd ~
git clone git@github.com:rmit-vietnam-computing-technologies/2026b-cosc2767-a1-<campus>-<your-github-username>-<student-id>.git

Task 9 — Edit README.md, commit + push to main → 1e.png
bash
cd 2026b-cosc2767-a1-<repo-name>
git config --global user.name "Full Name"
git config --global user.email "you@example.com"
nano README.md
Replace the project title and every bracketed placeholder with:
Course code
Assignment 1 - Mid-term Exam
[Full name]
[Student ID]
[GitHub username]

Save, then:

bash
git add README.md
git commit -m "Edit the README file"
git push

Task 10 — Create develop branch, question-1 folder → 1f.png
bash
git checkout -b develop
mkdir question-1
cp README.md question-1/
git add question-1
git commit -m "Set up develop branch and question-1 folder"
git push -u origin develop
